('127.481.d.10.I',3,'A chemical that carries a signal across a synapse from one neuron to the next is a:','["hormone", "antibody", "neurotransmitter", "enzyme"]'::jsonb,2,'Neurotransmitters cross the gap.','original'),
('127.481.d.10.I',4,'The neurotransmitter that stimulates skeletal muscle contraction is:','["melatonin", "serotonin", "insulin", "acetylcholine"]'::jsonb,3,'ACh acts at neuromuscular junctions.','original'),
('127.481.d.10.J',3,'A disease in which the myelin sheath of nerves is damaged, causing weakness and vision problems, is multiple:','["sclerosis", "stenosis", "dystrophy", "fibrosis"]'::jsonb,0,'MS is a demyelinating disease.','original'),
('127.481.d.10.J',4,'A sudden interruption of blood flow to part of the brain that can cause paralysis or speech loss is a:','["sprain", "stroke", "seizure only", "cramp"]'::jsonb,1,'A stroke damages brain tissue.','original'),
('127.481.d.11.A',3,'The pituitary gland, thyroid, adrenal glands, and pancreas are all part of the:','["respiratory system", "skeletal system", "endocrine system", "digestive system"]'::jsonb,2,'Endocrine glands secrete hormones.','original'),
('127.481.d.11.A',4,'The small gland at the base of the brain often called the master gland is the:','["thyroid", "thymus", "pineal gland", "pituitary gland"]'::jsonb,3,'The pituitary regulates other glands.','original'),
('127.481.d.11.B',3,'Glands that release their products directly into the bloodstream are:','["endocrine glands", "exocrine glands", "salivary glands", "sweat glands"]'::jsonb,0,'Endocrine glands are ductless.','original'),
('127.481.d.11.B',4,'Sweat glands and salivary glands release secretions through ducts, so they are:','["ductless glands", "exocrine glands", "pineal glands", "endocrine glands"]'::jsonb,1,'Exocrine glands use ducts.','original'),
('127.481.d.11.C',3,'The hormone from the pancreas that lowers blood sugar is:','["estrogen", "thyroxine", "insulin", "cortisol"]'::jsonb,2,'Insulin lowers glucose.','original'),
('127.481.d.11.C',4,'The thyroid gland produces thyroxine, a hormone that controls the body''s:','["hair color", "bone length", "eye color", "metabolic rate"]'::jsonb,3,'Thyroxine controls metabolism.','original'),
('127.481.d.11.D',3,'Insulin and glucagon work together to keep blood sugar in a narrow range, maintaining:','["homeostasis", "disease", "growth", "fatigue"]'::jsonb,0,'Hormones regulate homeostasis.','original'),
('127.481.d.11.D',4,'When blood calcium is low, parathyroid hormone raises it by pulling calcium from bone. This hormone helps keep the body''s calcium:','["unmeasured", "balanced", "unstable", "low"]'::jsonb,1,'PTH restores calcium balance.','original'),
('127.481.d.11.E',3,'A gland that is turned on by a signal from the brain is regulated by a:','["bone stimulus", "hormonal stimulus", "neural stimulus", "humoral stimulus"]'::jsonb,2,'Neural stimuli come from nerves.','original'),
('127.481.d.11.E',4,'When rising blood glucose directly triggers the pancreas to release insulin, the gland is regulated by a:','["skeletal stimulus", "hormonal stimulus", "neural stimulus", "humoral stimulus"]'::jsonb,3,'Humoral = blood chemistry.','original'),
('127.481.d.11.F',3,'A disease in which the body does not make enough insulin or cannot use it properly is:','["diabetes mellitus", "Graves disease", "goiter", "Addison disease"]'::jsonb,0,'Diabetes involves insulin problems.','original'),
('127.481.d.11.F',4,'An overactive thyroid gland, which can cause weight loss and a rapid heartbeat, is called:','["hypothyroidism", "hyperthyroidism", "dwarfism", "acromegaly"]'::jsonb,1,'Hyper means excess.','original'),
('127.481.d.12.A',3,'The organs that filter blood and make urine are the:','["ureters", "bladder", "kidneys", "urethra"]'::jsonb,2,'Kidneys filter blood.','original'),
('127.481.d.12.A',4,'Tubes that carry urine from the kidneys to the bladder are the:','["nephrons", "arteries", "urethra", "ureters"]'::jsonb,3,'Ureters move urine to the bladder.','original'),
('127.481.d.12.B',3,'Urine leaves the body through a tube called the:','["urethra", "ureter", "aorta", "trachea"]'::jsonb,0,'Urethra is the exit.','original'),
('127.481.d.12.B',4,'The urethra in males is longer than in females and also carries:','["lymph", "semen", "bile", "blood"]'::jsonb,1,'The male urethra is shared.','original'),
('127.481.d.12.C',3,'The microscopic filtering unit of a kidney is the:','["alveolus", "neuron", "nephron", "osteon"]'::jsonb,2,'Nephrons filter blood.','original'),
('127.481.d.12.C',4,'In a nephron, blood is first filtered in a cluster of capillaries called the:','["alveolus", "cochlea", "villus", "glomerulus"]'::jsonb,3,'The glomerulus filters.','original'),
('127.481.d.12.D',3,'The kidneys maintain fluid balance by adjusting how much water is kept or lost in:','["urine", "skin only", "hair", "bone"]'::jsonb,0,'Urine output regulates fluid.','original'),
('127.481.d.12.D',4,'The hormone ADH signals the kidneys to reabsorb more water, which helps the body avoid:','["digestion", "dehydration", "growth", "hydration"]'::jsonb,1,'ADH conserves water.','original'),
('127.481.d.12.E',3,'Normal urine is mostly water and also contains urea and:','["large proteins", "red blood cells", "salts", "glucose in large amounts"]'::jsonb,2,'Urine has dissolved wastes.','original'),
('127.481.d.12.E',4,'The three main steps of urine formation are filtration, reabsorption, and:','["digestion", "absorption only", "synthesis", "secretion"]'::jsonb,3,'Secretion adds wastes.','original'),
('127.481.d.12.F',3,'When blood pressure falls, the kidneys release renin, showing that the renal system works with the nervous system and:','["the endocrine system", "the skeletal system", "the integumentary system", "the digestive system only"]'::jsonb,0,'Renin-angiotensin integrates systems.','original'),
('127.481.d.12.F',4,'The adrenal hormone aldosterone helps the kidneys keep sodium and water, linking the renal and endocrine systems to control:','["skin color", "blood pressure", "bone density", "hair growth"]'::jsonb,1,'Aldosterone raises BP.','original'),
('127.481.d.12.G',3,'An infection of the bladder is called:','["hepatitis", "gastritis", "cystitis", "nephritis"]'::jsonb,2,'Cystitis is bladder infection.','original'),
('127.481.d.12.G',4,'Hard deposits of minerals that form in the kidney and can block the flow of urine are kidney:','["cysts only", "clots", "fibers", "stones"]'::jsonb,3,'Kidney stones obstruct flow.','original'),
('127.481.d.13.A',3,'The main function of the cardiovascular system is to transport oxygen, nutrients, and wastes by pumping:','["blood", "air", "bile", "food"]'::jsonb,0,'The heart pumps blood.','original'),
('127.481.d.13.A',4,'Besides transport, the cardiovascular system helps regulate body temperature and protect the body through white blood cells and:','["vision", "clotting", "hearing", "digestion"]'::jsonb,1,'Platelets clot blood.','original'),
('127.481.d.13.B',3,'Vessels that carry blood away from the heart are:','["veins", "valves", "arteries", "capillaries"]'::jsonb,2,'Arteries carry blood away.','original'),
('127.481.d.13.B',4,'The tiny vessels where oxygen and nutrients are exchanged with tissues are:','["venules", "veins", "arteries", "capillaries"]'::jsonb,3,'Capillaries exchange materials.','original'),
('127.481.d.13.C',3,'Systemic circulation carries oxygen-rich blood from the left side of the heart to the body and returns oxygen-poor blood to the:','["right atrium", "left atrium", "lungs directly", "left ventricle"]'::jsonb,0,'Systemic blood returns to the right atrium.','original'),
('127.481.d.13.C',4,'The largest artery that carries blood from the left ventricle to the body is the:','["vena cava", "aorta", "carotid artery", "pulmonary artery"]'::jsonb,1,'The aorta leaves the left ventricle.','original'),
('127.481.d.13.D',3,'If blood vessels narrow while the heart output stays the same, blood pressure will:','["fall", "disappear", "rise", "stop"]'::jsonb,2,'Resistance raises pressure.','original'),
('127.481.d.13.D',4,'Blood flows from areas of high pressure to areas of low pressure, so blood moves fastest where the pressure difference is:','["zero", "smallest", "constant", "greatest"]'::jsonb,3,'Gradient drives flow.','original'),
('127.481.d.13.E',3,'The circulation that supplies the heart muscle itself with blood is the:','["coronary circulation", "systemic circulation", "portal circulation", "pulmonary circulation"]'::jsonb,0,'Coronary arteries feed the heart.','original'),
('127.481.d.13.E',4,'Blood is carried to the lungs to pick up oxygen by the:','["cerebral circulation", "pulmonary circulation", "coronary circulation", "systemic circulation"]'::jsonb,1,'The pulmonary loop goes to the lungs.','original'),
('127.481.d.13.F',3,'On an electrocardiogram, the large spike that shows the ventricles contracting is the:','["T wave", "P wave", "QRS complex", "U wave"]'::jsonb,2,'QRS shows ventricular depolarization.','original'),
('127.481.d.13.F',4,'The P wave on an EKG represents the electrical activation of the:','["valves", "aorta", "ventricles", "atria"]'::jsonb,3,'P wave = atrial depolarization.','original'),
('127.481.d.13.G',3,'The part of the nervous system that speeds up the heart during exercise is the:','["sympathetic nervous system", "enteric system", "somatic nervous system", "parasympathetic nervous system"]'::jsonb,0,'Sympathetic raises heart rate.','original'),
('127.481.d.13.G',4,'The vagus nerve slows the heart, so it belongs to the:','["somatic division", "parasympathetic division", "skeletal division", "sympathetic division"]'::jsonb,1,'Parasympathetic slows the heart.','original'),
('127.481.d.13.H',3,'A condition in which arteries become narrowed and hardened by plaque is:','["anemia", "angina", "atherosclerosis", "arrhythmia"]'::jsonb,2,'Plaque narrows arteries.','original'),
('127.481.d.13.H',4,'A heart condition in which the heartbeat is irregular is called:','["hypertension", "atherosclerosis", "anemia", "arrhythmia"]'::jsonb,3,'Arrhythmia is abnormal rhythm.','original'),
('127.481.d.14.A',3,'The lymphatic system helps the cardiovascular system by returning excess tissue fluid to the:','["bloodstream", "stomach", "skin", "skull"]'::jsonb,0,'Lymph drains back into blood.','original'),
('127.481.d.14.A',4,'Lymphatic vessels in the intestines absorb dietary fats, showing the lymphatic system also works with the:','["urinary system", "digestive system", "integumentary system", "skeletal system"]'::jsonb,1,'Lacteals absorb fat.','original'),
('127.481.d.14.B',3,'Small bean-shaped organs that filter lymph and house immune cells are lymph:','["ducts", "valves", "nodes", "vessels"]'::jsonb,2,'Lymph nodes filter lymph.','original'),
('127.481.d.14.B',4,'The lymphatic organ in the upper left abdomen that filters blood and stores platelets is the:','["appendix", "tonsil", "thymus", "spleen"]'::jsonb,3,'The spleen filters blood.','original'),
('127.481.d.14.C',3,'White blood cells that make antibodies are:','["B lymphocytes", "platelets", "neurons", "red blood cells"]'::jsonb,0,'B cells make antibodies.','original'),
('127.481.d.14.C',4,'White blood cells that engulf and digest bacteria by phagocytosis include:','["platelets", "macrophages", "osteoclasts", "erythrocytes"]'::jsonb,1,'Macrophages are phagocytes.','original'),
('127.481.d.14.D',3,'A person with type A blood has A antigens on their red blood cells and has antibodies against type:','["A", "O antigens only", "B", "AB"]'::jsonb,2,'Type A makes anti-B.','original'),
('127.481.d.14.D',4,'People with type O negative blood are called universal donors for red blood cells because their cells lack:','["all proteins", "hemoglobin", "iron", "A, B, and Rh antigens"]'::jsonb,3,'No A, B, or Rh antigens to react.','original'),
('127.481.d.14.E',3,'The skin and mucous membranes protect the body from germs as the first line of defense, which is part of nonspecific:','["immunity", "growth", "digestion", "hunger"]'::jsonb,0,'Barriers are nonspecific.','original')
