('127.481.d.15.C',3,'Excess glucose is stored in the liver and muscles as:','["bile", "insulin", "glycogen", "cholesterol"]'::jsonb,2,'Glycogen stores glucose.','original'),
('127.481.d.15.C',4,'When the body has more energy than it needs, extra calories can be stored in adipose tissue as:','["skin", "muscle protein", "bone", "fat"]'::jsonb,3,'Fat is stored energy.','original'),
('127.481.d.15.D',3,'Stomach acid backing up into the esophagus and causing heartburn is called gastroesophageal reflux disease, or:','["GERD", "IBS", "COPD", "ALS"]'::jsonb,0,'GERD is acid reflux.','original'),
('127.481.d.15.D',4,'An inflammation of the liver, often caused by a virus, is:','["nephritis", "hepatitis", "gastritis", "colitis"]'::jsonb,1,'Hepat means liver.','original'),
('127.481.d.16.A',3,'Air entering through the nose travels through the pharynx, larynx, trachea, bronchi, and finally reaches the tiny air sacs called:','["villi", "glomeruli", "alveoli", "nephrons"]'::jsonb,2,'Alveoli are the exchange sites.','original'),
('127.481.d.16.A',4,'The structure that closes over the trachea during swallowing to keep food out of the airway is the:','["uvula", "larynx wall", "tonsil", "epiglottis"]'::jsonb,3,'The epiglottis covers the glottis.','original'),
('127.481.d.16.B',3,'The nose, pharynx, and larynx make up the upper respiratory tract, which warms, moistens, and filters the:','["air", "food", "urine", "blood"]'::jsonb,0,'Upper tract conditions air.','original'),
('127.481.d.16.B',4,'The trachea, bronchi, and lungs make up the lower respiratory tract, where the main job is:','["hearing", "gas exchange", "digestion", "balance"]'::jsonb,1,'Lower tract exchanges gases.','original'),
('127.481.d.16.C',3,'The movement of air into and out of the lungs is called pulmonary:','["circulation", "digestion", "ventilation", "filtration"]'::jsonb,2,'Ventilation is breathing.','original'),
('127.481.d.16.C',4,'The exchange of oxygen and carbon dioxide between the blood and body cells is called:','["ventilation", "expiration", "external respiration", "internal respiration"]'::jsonb,3,'Internal respiration happens at tissues.','original'),
('127.481.d.16.D',3,'Red blood cells carry oxygen from the lungs to the body, showing the respiratory system works closely with the:','["cardiovascular system", "skeletal system", "integumentary system", "urinary system"]'::jsonb,0,'Oxygen is transported by blood.','original'),
('127.481.d.16.D',4,'Oxygen binds to the protein in red blood cells called:','["keratin", "hemoglobin", "myosin", "collagen"]'::jsonb,1,'Hemoglobin carries oxygen.','original'),
('127.481.d.16.E',3,'During exercise, breathing rate increases because muscles need more oxygen and produce more carbon dioxide, which stimulates the:','["skin", "stomach", "respiratory center in the brain", "kidneys"]'::jsonb,2,'CO2 drives breathing rate.','original'),
('127.481.d.16.E',4,'At high altitude, the air has less oxygen, so a person may breathe faster to maintain adequate oxygen:','["in the stomach", "in the shoes", "on the skin", "levels in the blood"]'::jsonb,3,'Altitude affects respiration.','original'),
('127.481.d.16.F',3,'A chronic disease in which airways become inflamed and narrow, causing wheezing, is:','["asthma", "pneumonia", "emphysema", "tuberculosis"]'::jsonb,0,'Asthma narrows airways.','original'),
('127.481.d.16.F',4,'An infection of the lungs in which the alveoli fill with fluid is:','["sinusitis", "pneumonia", "asthma", "bronchitis only"]'::jsonb,1,'Pneumonia fills air sacs.','original'),
('127.481.d.17.A',3,'The early embryo develops three primary germ layers that go on to form all tissues and organs. The process is called embryological:','["repair", "decay", "development", "starvation"]'::jsonb,2,'Germ layers differentiate.','original'),
('127.481.d.17.A',4,'The germ layer that gives rise to the skin and nervous system is the:','["endoderm", "myoderm", "mesoderm", "ectoderm"]'::jsonb,3,'Ectoderm forms skin and nerves.','original'),
('127.481.d.17.B',3,'The female organs that produce egg cells are the:','["ovaries", "fallopian tubes", "testes", "uterus"]'::jsonb,0,'Ovaries produce ova.','original'),
('127.481.d.17.B',4,'The male organs that produce sperm and the hormone testosterone are the:','["prostate", "testes", "ovaries", "seminal vesicles"]'::jsonb,1,'Testes produce sperm.','original'),
('127.481.d.17.C',3,'The process of forming sperm cells is called:','["oogenesis", "fertilization", "spermatogenesis", "mitosis"]'::jsonb,2,'Spermatogenesis makes sperm.','original'),
('127.481.d.17.C',4,'The process of forming egg cells in the ovary is called:','["meiosis only", "spermatogenesis", "fission", "oogenesis"]'::jsonb,3,'Oogenesis makes eggs.','original'),
('127.481.d.17.D',3,'The hormone estrogen, produced mainly in the ovaries, influences the female:','["reproductive cycle", "digestive cycle", "water cycle", "sleep cycle"]'::jsonb,0,'Estrogen drives the cycle.','original'),
('127.481.d.17.D',4,'A surge of luteinizing hormone triggers the release of an egg from the ovary in a process called:','["implantation", "ovulation", "menstruation", "fertilization"]'::jsonb,1,'LH surge triggers ovulation.','original'),
('127.481.d.17.E',3,'During puberty in males, the hormone that causes a deeper voice and facial hair is:','["oxytocin", "estrogen", "testosterone", "insulin"]'::jsonb,2,'Testosterone drives male traits.','original'),
('127.481.d.17.E',4,'The pituitary hormones FSH and LH help control maturation of the reproductive organs and are called:','["thyrotropins", "catecholamines", "mineralocorticoids", "gonadotropins"]'::jsonb,3,'FSH and LH stimulate gonads.','original'),
('127.481.d.17.F',3,'A sexually transmitted infection caused by a bacterium that can be treated with antibiotics is:','["chlamydia", "mumps", "influenza", "measles"]'::jsonb,0,'Chlamydia is bacterial.','original'),
('127.481.d.17.F',4,'A condition in which uterine-like tissue grows outside the uterus, causing pain, is:','["gastritis", "endometriosis", "osteoporosis", "emphysema"]'::jsonb,1,'Endometriosis is a reproductive disorder.','original'),
('127.481.d.18.A',3,'Replacing a failed kidney with one from a donor is an advance in medicine at the organ level called an organ:','["lift", "search", "transplant", "cure"]'::jsonb,2,'Transplants replace organs.','original'),
('127.481.d.18.A',4,'A machine that takes over the work of the heart and lungs during surgery is a heart-lung:','["microscope", "scale", "radio", "bypass machine"]'::jsonb,3,'Bypass machines support circulation.','original'),
('127.481.d.18.B',3,'Treating disease by changing a person''s genes at the cellular level is called gene:','["therapy", "cloning", "farming", "mapping"]'::jsonb,0,'Gene therapy alters cells.','original'),
('127.481.d.18.B',4,'Stem cells are valuable in medicine because they can develop into many types of:','["fabrics", "specialized cells", "rocks", "metals"]'::jsonb,1,'Stem cells differentiate.','original'),
('127.482.d.1.A',3,'A student reads a case study in which several patients all develop rashes after eating at the same restaurant and asks what could cause it. This is forming a:','["prescription", "treatment plan", "testable question", "diagnosis"]'::jsonb,2,'Observations lead to questions.','original'),
('127.482.d.1.A',4,'In a pathology investigation, defining the problem includes stating what is unknown and which patient characteristics will be:','["hidden", "erased", "ignored", "compared"]'::jsonb,3,'Problems define variables.','original'),
('127.482.d.1.B',3,'An investigation that observes patients without changing anything, such as recording symptoms of a disease over time, is:','["descriptive", "experimental", "comparative", "controlled"]'::jsonb,0,'Descriptive studies record.','original'),
('127.482.d.1.B',4,'A study that compares smokers and nonsmokers for lung disease rates is a:','["model", "comparative investigation", "descriptive log", "hypothesis"]'::jsonb,1,'Groups are compared.','original'),
('127.482.d.1.C',3,'A lab worker handling a blood sample should wear gloves and treat the sample as potentially infectious by using:','["open containers", "bare hands", "standard precautions", "no precautions"]'::jsonb,2,'Standard precautions protect workers.','original'),
('127.482.d.1.C',4,'When a dropper of culture spills on the lab bench, the first step is to put on gloves and:','["leave it", "wipe it with a dry tissue", "blow on it", "cover and disinfect the spill"]'::jsonb,3,'Disinfect spills.','original'),
('127.482.d.1.D',3,'A spreadsheet program helps organize patient lab values so that a student can calculate:','["averages", "prescriptions", "insurance", "diagnoses"]'::jsonb,0,'Software supports calculations.','original'),
('127.482.d.1.D',4,'Data-collecting probes, calculators, and spreadsheets are examples of tools used to collect and analyze:','["comics", "scientific data", "menus", "fashion"]'::jsonb,1,'Tools gather data.','original'),
('127.482.d.1.E',3,'A patient''s temperature in a research lab is recorded in degrees:','["Rankine", "Fahrenheit", "Celsius", "Kelvin only"]'::jsonb,2,'SI-friendly units use Celsius.','original'),
