from (values
('127.482.d.1.H',3,'The idea that microorganisms cause many diseases is supported by a large body of evidence. In science, such a well-supported explanation is called a:','["theory", "law only", "guess", "rumor"]'::jsonb,0,'Germ theory is a theory.','original'),
('127.482.d.1.H',4,'A statement that a certain bacterium causes a disease, written before testing, is a:','["conclusion", "hypothesis", "law", "theory"]'::jsonb,1,'A hypothesis is testable.','original'),
('127.482.d.2.A',3,'Using mice to model human disease has the advantage of being cheap and quick but the limitation that mice are not exactly like:','["fish", "rats", "people", "insects"]'::jsonb,2,'Model limits.','original'),
('127.482.d.2.A',4,'A computer model of heart disease is limited by the data and assumptions that went into building its:','["logo", "title", "font", "design"]'::jsonb,3,'Models are simplified.','original'),
('127.482.d.2.B',3,'A scientist sees that cases of influenza rise in winter and fall in summer. She has identified a:','["seasonal pattern", "calculation error", "new species", "fossil"]'::jsonb,0,'Patterns in data.','original'),
('127.482.d.2.B',4,'A graph of the number of new cases each week for a year shows a sharp spike. A scientist would analyze this as a statistical:','["mistake", "feature of the data", "decoration", "law"]'::jsonb,1,'Spikes are features.','original'),
('127.482.d.2.C',3,'If 8 of 200 people in a town have a disease, the percentage with the disease is:','["16 percent", "8 percent", "4 percent", "25 percent"]'::jsonb,2,'8 / 200 = 0.04.','original'),
('127.482.d.2.C',4,'A virus population doubles every 3 hours. Starting with 50 particles, after 9 hours there will be:','["150", "450", "200", "400"]'::jsonb,3,'50 x 2 x 2 x 2 = 400.','original'),
('127.482.d.2.D',3,'Comparing a new test for infection against the older test to see if it is accurate is evaluating an experimental:','["design", "opinion", "slogan", "logo"]'::jsonb,0,'Designs are evaluated.','original'),
('127.482.d.2.D',4,'A hospital tests a new hand-washing station to see if infection rates drop. This is evaluating an engineering:','["fashion", "design", "policy name", "menu"]'::jsonb,1,'Engineering designs are evaluated with outcomes.','original'),
('127.482.d.3.A',3,'A student explains why a patient has swelling and supports the explanation with lab results and an inflammation model. The explanation is supported by:','["guesses", "rumors", "data and models", "opinion"]'::jsonb,2,'Evidence supports explanations.','original'),
('127.482.d.3.A',4,'A proposed solution for reducing hospital infections is stronger when data show that infection rates:','["rose", "were not measured", "stayed the same", "fell after the change"]'::jsonb,3,'Data show effectiveness.','original'),
('127.482.d.3.B',3,'Researchers share study results with other scientists by writing reports and giving presentations. This is:','["communication", "guessing", "delay", "secrecy"]'::jsonb,0,'Communicating results.','original'),
('127.482.d.3.B',4,'In a group project on disease prevention, students assign roles, share findings, and combine their ideas. This is:','["competition", "collaboration", "avoidance", "conflict"]'::jsonb,1,'Teamwork.','original'),
('127.482.d.3.C',3,'During a debate about a vaccine study, a respectful scientist responds to a challenge by:','["walking away", "shouting", "citing evidence", "insulting"]'::jsonb,2,'Argue with evidence.','original'),
('127.482.d.3.C',4,'When two researchers disagree on a study''s conclusion, they can resolve the disagreement by:','["ignoring each other", "guessing", "hiding the study", "reexamining the data"]'::jsonb,3,'Review the evidence.','original'),
('127.482.d.4.A',3,'To evaluate a news article claiming a food cures cancer, a student checks the article''s:','["evidence", "length", "headline only", "font"]'::jsonb,0,'Evidence is key.','original'),
('127.482.d.4.A',4,'A study about a drug has only five patients and no control group. A critic would conclude that the study''s explanation is:','["proven", "weak", "certain", "perfect"]'::jsonb,1,'Small, uncontrolled studies are weak.','original'),
('127.482.d.4.B',3,'John Snow traced a cholera outbreak to a contaminated water pump, which changed thinking about how disease:','["heals", "looks", "spreads", "feels"]'::jsonb,2,'Snow''s work founded epidemiology.','original'),
('127.482.d.4.B',4,'The discovery of penicillin changed the treatment of bacterial infections and led to the field of:','["aviation", "geology", "astronomy", "antibiotics"]'::jsonb,3,'Penicillin began the antibiotic era.','original'),
('127.482.d.4.C',3,'A student interested in pathology could learn about careers from a university department or a:','["professional society", "shopping website", "gossip site", "game"]'::jsonb,0,'Reliable career sources.','original'),
('127.482.d.4.C',4,'Libraries and medical museums help students research the history of:','["sports", "disease and medicine", "fashion", "cooking"]'::jsonb,1,'Resources aid research.','original'),
('127.482.d.5.A',3,'Abnormal changes at the cellular level, such as swelling or shrinking of cells, are the starting point of many:','["games", "recipes", "diseases", "fashions"]'::jsonb,2,'Cell injury underlies disease.','original'),
('127.482.d.5.A',4,'A cell that is injured and cannot recover will undergo cell death, which may be programmed, called apoptosis, or caused by injury, called:','["osmosis", "mitosis", "meiosis", "necrosis"]'::jsonb,3,'Necrosis is death from injury.','original'),
('127.482.d.5.B',3,'A change in the DNA sequence of a gene is a:','["mutation", "translation", "fusion", "hormone"]'::jsonb,0,'Mutations alter DNA.','original'),
('127.482.d.5.B',4,'An abnormal mass of tissue that forms when cells divide uncontrollably is a:','["nucleus", "neoplasm", "nephron", "neuron"]'::jsonb,1,'Neoplasms are new growths.','original'),
('127.482.d.5.C',3,'Factors that contribute to the risk of disease include age, gender, genetics, and:','["favorite color", "birthday cake", "lifestyle", "shoe size"]'::jsonb,2,'Lifestyle affects risk.','original'),
('127.482.d.5.C',4,'A person whose family has a history of heart disease has an increased risk because of a factor called:','["nationality only", "hobby", "rumor", "heredity"]'::jsonb,3,'Heredity influences disease.','original'),
('127.482.d.5.D',3,'When blood loss lowers blood pressure, the heart rate rises to maintain circulation. This is a compensating mechanism that tries to restore:','["homeostasis", "injury", "infection", "illness"]'::jsonb,0,'Compensation protects balance.','original'),
('127.482.d.5.D',4,'If the body cannot compensate, as in severe blood loss, the result may be a life-threatening condition called:','["itching", "shock", "fatigue", "sneezing"]'::jsonb,1,'Failure to compensate causes shock.','original'),
('127.482.d.6.A',3,'A Gram stain separates bacteria into two groups based on the structure of their:','["nuclei", "ribosomes", "cell walls", "flagella"]'::jsonb,2,'Gram stain reveals cell wall type.','original'),
('127.482.d.6.A',4,'Spherical bacteria are called cocci and rod-shaped bacteria are called:','["vibrios", "spirilla", "amoebae", "bacilli"]'::jsonb,3,'Bacilli are rods.','original'),
('127.482.d.6.B',3,'The stage of pathogenesis after exposure and before symptoms begin is the:','["incubation period", "convalescence", "recovery period", "acute stage"]'::jsonb,0,'Incubation precedes symptoms.','original'),
('127.482.d.6.B',4,'The stage of a disease when symptoms are at their worst is the:','["incubation period", "acute stage", "prodromal stage", "convalescent stage"]'::jsonb,1,'Acute stage peaks.','original'),
('127.482.d.6.C',3,'The skin, mucous membranes, and stomach acid are barriers that make up the body''s natural:','["weak points", "hormones", "defense systems", "food sources"]'::jsonb,2,'Barriers defend against infection.','original'),
('127.482.d.6.C',4,'White blood cells that engulf pathogens are part of the body''s natural defense against:','["sleep", "growth", "hunger", "infection"]'::jsonb,3,'Phagocytes fight infection.','original'),
('127.482.d.6.D',3,'A preparation that trains the immune system to recognize a pathogen so that the person does not get the disease is a:','["vaccine", "analgesic", "antibiotic", "antacid"]'::jsonb,0,'Vaccines prevent disease.','original'),
('127.482.d.6.D',4,'Drugs that kill or stop the growth of bacteria are:','["vaccines", "antibiotics", "antivirals", "vitamins"]'::jsonb,1,'Antibiotics treat bacterial infection.','original'),
('127.482.d.6.E',3,'Exposure to asbestos, smoke, and other pollution can cause disease by damaging the cells of the:','["bones only", "hair", "lungs", "nails"]'::jsonb,2,'Pollutants harm lungs.','original'),
('127.482.d.6.E',4,'Radiation, certain chemicals, and some viruses can cause cancer because they can damage the cell''s:','["hair", "shell", "skin", "DNA"]'::jsonb,3,'Carcinogens damage DNA.','original'),
('127.482.d.7.A',3,'Doctors study the cause of a disease, its signs and symptoms, how it is diagnosed, and how it is likely to progress. The cause is called its:','["etiology", "anatomy", "pathology", "prognosis"]'::jsonb,0,'Etiology means cause.','original'),
('127.482.d.7.A',4,'The expected course and outcome of a disease is called its:','["symptom", "prognosis", "etiology", "diagnosis"]'::jsonb,1,'Prognosis predicts outcome.','original'),
('127.482.d.7.B',3,'An imaging technique that uses magnetic fields and radio waves to make detailed pictures of soft tissue is:','["X-ray", "EKG", "MRI", "ultrasound"]'::jsonb,2,'MRI images soft tissue.','original'),
('127.482.d.7.B',4,'Using a small camera on a flexible tube to look inside the digestive tract is called:','["biopsy", "transfusion", "dialysis", "endoscopy"]'::jsonb,3,'Endoscopy views internal organs.','original'),
('127.482.d.7.C',3,'Diseases such as malaria and tuberculosis have reemerged in some regions partly because of drug-resistant strains and:','["travel and poverty", "vaccines for all", "fewer people", "better sanitation"]'::jsonb,0,'Reemergence has several causes.','original'),
('127.482.d.7.C',4,'A disease that was once controlled and then returns is called a:','["chronic disease", "reemerging disease", "new disease", "genetic disease"]'::jsonb,1,'Reemerging means it returned.','original'),
('127.482.d.7.D',3,'An infection that a patient acquires during a stay in a hospital is called a:','["genetic infection", "congenital infection", "nosocomial infection", "chronic infection"]'::jsonb,2,'Nosocomial = hospital-acquired.','original'),
('127.482.d.7.D',4,'The most important and simple way to prevent the spread of infections in hospitals is proper:','["air freshening", "wearing jewelry", "painting walls", "hand washing"]'::jsonb,3,'Hand hygiene prevents spread.','original'),
('127.482.d.7.E',3,'Bacteria that no longer respond to common antibiotics, such as MRSA, are called antibiotic-:','["resistant", "dependent", "sensitive", "friendly"]'::jsonb,0,'MRSA resists methicillin.','original'),
('127.482.d.7.E',4,'Antibiotic resistance increases when people take antibiotics for viral infections or do not complete:','["a lunch break", "the prescribed course", "an exercise plan", "a shopping trip"]'::jsonb,1,'Misuse creates resistance.','original'),
('127.482.d.7.F',3,'A disease that is present at birth, such as cystic fibrosis, is called:','["acquired", "idiopathic", "congenital", "iatrogenic"]'::jsonb,2,'Congenital means from birth.','original'),
('127.482.d.7.F',4,'A disease with a sudden onset and a short duration, such as the flu, is:','["degenerative", "chronic", "congenital", "acute"]'::jsonb,3,'Acute is short and sudden.','original'),
('127.482.d.7.G',3,'Diseases such as lupus and multiple sclerosis involve the immune system attacking the body''s own cells, so they are called:','["autoimmune diseases", "infectious diseases", "traumatic injuries", "nutritional diseases"]'::jsonb,0,'Autoimmunity is self-attack.','original'),
('127.482.d.7.G',4,'Diabetes and Parkinson''s disease can be managed over years with treatment and lifestyle changes, which is characteristic of a:','["wound", "chronic disease", "acute disease", "poisoning"]'::jsonb,1,'Chronic diseases last long.','original'),
('127.482.d.8.A',3,'A practice that keeps an area free from germs is called:','["antisepsis only", "contamination", "asepsis", "sepsis"]'::jsonb,2,'Asepsis prevents infection.','original')
) as v(code, diff, prompt, choices, ans, expl, src)
join public.teks_items i on i.code = v.code and i.is_standard
join public.teks_documents d on d.id = i.document_id and d.subject = 'Career Development' and d.language = 'en'
on conflict (fingerprint) do nothing;
insert into public.question_bank (teks_code, teks_item_id, subject, grade_num, course, difficulty, qtype, prompt, choices, answer_idx, explanation, source, status, gen_batch)
select distinct on (v.prompt) v.code, i.id, d.subject,
       case when i.grade_level = 'K' then 0 when i.grade_level ~ '^[0-9]+' then substring(i.grade_level from '^[0-9]+')::smallint end,
       case when i.grade_level is null then i.grade_course_title end,
       v.diff, 'mc', v.prompt, v.choices, v.ans, v.expl, v.src, 'checked', 'cte_71_v1'
from (values
('127.482.d.8.A',4,'Separating patients who have a contagious disease from other people to prevent spread is:','["immunization", "transfusion", "rehabilitation", "isolation"]'::jsonb,3,'Isolation limits spread.','original'),
('127.482.d.8.B',3,'Long-term stress can weaken the immune system and raise the risk of:','["illness", "height", "strength", "growth"]'::jsonb,0,'Chronic stress hurts health.','original'),
('127.482.d.8.B',4,'With aging, bones lose density and skin loses elasticity, which are changes in body:','["addresses", "structure and function", "colors", "names"]'::jsonb,1,'Aging changes the body.','original'),
('127.482.d.8.C',3,'A lab report shows a patient''s white blood cell count is much higher than the normal range. This most likely indicates:','["hunger", "normal health", "an infection", "a broken bone"]'::jsonb,2,'High WBC suggests infection.','original'),
('127.482.d.8.C',4,'A fasting blood glucose reading well above the reference range is interpreted as a possible sign of:','["asthma", "anemia", "arthritis", "diabetes"]'::jsonb,3,'High glucose suggests diabetes.','original'),
('127.482.d.8.D',3,'Epidemiologists collect data on how many people get a disease and where. This type of data helps identify:','["trends", "names", "colors", "songs"]'::jsonb,0,'Epidemiological data show trends.','original'),
('127.482.d.8.D',4,'A graph showing flu cases climbing each week for a month suggests a growing:','["recovery", "outbreak", "budget", "vaccine"]'::jsonb,1,'Rising cases show an outbreak.','original'),
('127.482.d.8.E',3,'Diseases such as HIV and tuberculosis threaten world health, and a good plan to reduce them would include education, access to treatment, and:','["neglect", "denial", "prevention", "delay"]'::jsonb,2,'Prevention is key.','original'),
('127.482.d.8.E',4,'To address a disease that threatens world health, groups such as the World Health Organization help countries with surveillance, vaccination, and:','["tourism ads", "fashion shows", "sports leagues", "health education"]'::jsonb,3,'Global solutions include education.','original'),
('127.482.d.8.F',3,'A prevention plan for heart disease might include eating a healthy diet, not smoking, and getting regular:','["exercise", "bed rest only", "sugary drinks", "fast food"]'::jsonb,0,'Behavior affects risk.','original'),
('127.482.d.8.F',4,'A plan to reduce lung cancer risk focuses on a behavior that contributes strongly to the disease:','["eating fruit", "avoiding tobacco", "watching television", "drinking water"]'::jsonb,1,'Tobacco is a major cause.','original'),
('127.483.d.1.A',3,'A pharmacy technician greets every customer politely and listens without judging. This shows a respectful and professional:','["uniform", "budget", "attitude", "schedule"]'::jsonb,2,'Professionalism builds trust.','original'),
('127.483.d.1.A',4,'A customer is upset about waiting for a refill. The best technician response is to stay calm, apologize for the delay, and:','["walk away", "ignore the customer", "argue back", "offer to help"]'::jsonb,3,'De-escalate and help.','original'),
('127.483.d.1.B',3,'When speaking with an older adult who has difficulty hearing, a technician should face the person, speak clearly, and:','["avoid shouting", "shout", "mumble", "turn away"]'::jsonb,0,'Adapt communication to the person.','original'),
('127.483.d.1.B',4,'To communicate with a patient who speaks little English, a pharmacy can use an interpreter service and simple, clear:','["abbreviations", "written instructions", "jargon", "slang"]'::jsonb,1,'Clear instructions help.','original'),
('127.483.d.2.A',3,'In a pharmacy, the abbreviation tab on a prescription means:','["tube", "table", "tablet", "tablespoon"]'::jsonb,2,'tab = tablet.','original'),
('127.483.d.2.A',4,'The abbreviation gtt on a prescription means:','["gram", "grain", "gallon", "drop"]'::jsonb,3,'gtt = drops.','original'),
('127.483.d.2.B',3,'A pharmacy that fills prescriptions for the general public, such as a drugstore, is a community pharmacy, while one inside a hospital is an:','["institutional pharmacy", "online pharmacy", "retail pharmacy", "vet pharmacy"]'::jsonb,0,'Hospital pharmacies are institutional.','original'),
('127.483.d.2.B',4,'In an institutional pharmacy, medication is often ordered with a medication order, while in a community pharmacy a patient brings a:','["coupon", "prescription", "receipt", "badge"]'::jsonb,1,'Terms differ by setting.','original'),
('127.483.d.2.C',3,'The sig code q.d. on a prescription means to take the medicine:','["every hour", "at night only", "once a day", "twice a day"]'::jsonb,2,'q.d. = daily.','original'),
('127.483.d.2.C',4,'The sig code b.i.d. on a prescription means to take the medicine:','["every other day", "once a day", "four times a day", "twice a day"]'::jsonb,3,'b.i.d. = twice daily.','original'),
('127.483.d.3.A',3,'Medications that can harm workers, such as chemotherapy drugs, must be handled and thrown away as:','["hazardous waste", "recycling", "compost", "ordinary trash"]'::jsonb,0,'Hazardous drugs need special disposal.','original'),
('127.483.d.3.A',4,'Unused non-hazardous medications cannot just be thrown in the regular trash in a pharmacy. They are usually sent through a reverse distributor or approved:','["gift program", "disposal program", "sale", "drain"]'::jsonb,1,'Proper disposal prevents harm.','original'),
('127.483.d.3.B',3,'A prescription for a Schedule II drug generally cannot be refilled and must include the prescriber''s signature and the patient''s:','["bank balance", "pet''s name", "name and address", "favorite color"]'::jsonb,2,'Controlled substance rules are strict.','original'),
('127.483.d.3.B',4,'The federal agency that regulates controlled substances is the Drug Enforcement:','["Association", "Alliance", "Authority", "Administration"]'::jsonb,3,'The DEA.','original'),
('127.483.d.3.C',3,'When the FDA finds that a medicine may be harmful, it can ask for a:','["recall", "discount", "sale", "promotion"]'::jsonb,0,'Recalls remove unsafe products.','original'),
('127.483.d.3.C',4,'A Class I recall is the most serious type and is used when a product could cause serious harm or:','["confusion", "death", "delay", "boredom"]'::jsonb,1,'Class I risks serious harm.','original'),
('127.483.d.3.D',3,'Statutes passed by state and federal governments affect how a pharmacy dispenses medication. A technician must be able to interpret and apply these:','["trends", "fashions", "laws", "rumors"]'::jsonb,2,'Laws guide practice.','original'),
('127.483.d.3.D',4,'A pharmacy follows the Health Insurance Portability and Accountability Act to protect patients'':','["paperwork", "pricing", "parking", "privacy"]'::jsonb,3,'HIPAA protects health information.','original'),
('127.483.d.3.E',3,'State and federal regulations about pharmacy practice tell technicians what tasks they may perform under the supervision of a:','["pharmacist", "clerk", "cashier", "manager"]'::jsonb,0,'Technicians work under a pharmacist.','original'),
('127.483.d.3.E',4,'Rules limit how many pharmacy technicians a pharmacist may supervise at one time, called the pharmacist-to-technician:','["salary", "ratio", "schedule", "discount"]'::jsonb,1,'Ratios are set by law.','original'),
('127.483.d.3.F',3,'A pharmacy follows professional standards and legal rules, which is called:','["negligence", "defiance", "compliance", "avoidance"]'::jsonb,2,'Compliance means following rules.','original'),
('127.483.d.3.F',4,'Keeping accurate records, checking IDs for controlled substances, and storing drugs securely are all part of pharmacy:','["decoration", "entertainment", "advertising", "compliance"]'::jsonb,3,'Compliance protects patients.','original'),
('127.483.d.4.A',3,'Tylenol is a brand name, and its generic name is:','["acetaminophen", "aspirin", "ibuprofen", "naproxen"]'::jsonb,0,'Tylenol is acetaminophen.','original'),
('127.483.d.4.A',4,'A medicine''s classification, such as antihypertensive, tells what group it belongs to, while its indication tells what it is used to:','["store", "treat", "sell", "cost"]'::jsonb,1,'Indication means use.','original'),
('127.483.d.4.B',3,'A condition in which a drug should not be used because it could cause harm to a patient is a:','["refill", "prescription", "contraindication", "indication"]'::jsonb,2,'Contraindications mean do not use.','original'),
('127.483.d.4.B',4,'When two medicines taken together change each other''s effects, the problem is called a drug:','["dose", "label", "recall", "interaction"]'::jsonb,3,'Interactions can be dangerous.','original'),
('127.483.d.4.C',3,'Medicines such as warfarin and digoxin have a narrow therapeutic index, which means the safe dose range is:','["small", "endless", "unimportant", "large"]'::jsonb,0,'NTI drugs need care.','original'),
('127.483.d.4.C',4,'Because the difference between a helpful and a harmful dose is tiny for an NTI drug, patients on these medications need careful:','["discounts", "monitoring", "advertising", "parking"]'::jsonb,1,'NTI drugs are monitored.','original'),
('127.483.d.4.D',3,'A technician who needs standards for compounding sterile preparations would look in a reference such as the United States:','["Telephone Book", "Postal Guide", "Pharmacopeia", "Almanac"]'::jsonb,2,'USP provides standards.','original'),
('127.483.d.4.D',4,'The reference book that lists FDA-approved drugs with therapeutic equivalence ratings is nicknamed the:','["Green Book", "Red Book", "Blue Book", "Orange Book"]'::jsonb,3,'The Orange Book lists equivalents.','original'),
('127.483.d.5.A',3,'A complete prescription includes the patient''s name, the drug name, the strength, the directions, and the prescriber''s:','["signature", "phone model", "hobby", "hat size"]'::jsonb,0,'Completeness is checked.','original'),
('127.483.d.5.A',4,'A prescription that does not list the drug strength is incomplete, so the technician should ask the pharmacist to contact the:','["insurance clerk", "prescriber", "patient''s neighbor", "delivery driver"]'::jsonb,1,'Clarify with the prescriber.','original'),
('127.483.d.5.B',3,'To enter a new customer''s prescription, the technician collects the patient''s name, date of birth, address, and:','["favorite food", "shoe size", "insurance information", "pet''s name"]'::jsonb,2,'Demographics and insurance are needed.','original'),
('127.483.d.5.B',4,'The technician should also ask a new patient about allergies, because this information can help the pharmacist avoid a harmful:','["delay", "discount", "refill", "reaction"]'::jsonb,3,'Allergy info protects safety.','original'),
('127.483.d.5.C',3,'When assisting the pharmacist in collecting a patient''s medication history, a technician records the medicines the patient takes and any:','["allergies", "hobbies", "vacations", "birthdays"]'::jsonb,0,'Allergies are key.','original'),
('127.483.d.5.C',4,'Recording over-the-counter drugs and supplements in the patient profile helps the pharmacist screen for:','["holidays", "interactions", "hobbies", "coupons"]'::jsonb,1,'OTC drugs can interact.','original'),
('127.483.d.5.D',3,'A prescription says take 1 tablet three times a day for 10 days. The total number of tablets to dispense is:','["10", "3", "30", "13"]'::jsonb,2,'1 x 3 x 10 = 30.','original'),
('127.483.d.5.D',4,'A prescription for a liquid says take 5 mL twice a day for 7 days. The total volume to dispense is:','["14 mL", "35 mL", "12 mL", "70 mL"]'::jsonb,3,'5 x 2 x 7 = 70.','original'),
('127.483.d.5.E',3,'Items such as glucose meters, test strips, and lancets are examples of:','["diabetic supplies", "toys", "office supplies", "cleaning products"]'::jsonb,0,'Diabetic supplies are sold in pharmacies.','original'),
('127.483.d.5.E',4,'A spacer is a device that attaches to an inhaler so that the patient gets more of the medication into the:','["stomach", "lungs", "eyes", "skin"]'::jsonb,1,'Spacers improve delivery.','original'),
('127.483.d.5.F',3,'A lot number on a medicine package helps the pharmacy find which products are affected during a:','["survey", "sale", "recall", "parade"]'::jsonb,2,'Lot numbers trace products.','original'),
('127.483.d.5.F',4,'The expiration date on a medication tells the pharmacy when the drug should no longer be:','["stored in a refrigerator", "labeled", "counted", "used or dispensed"]'::jsonb,3,'Expired drugs are removed.','original'),
('127.483.d.5.G',3,'A technician practices infection control by washing hands before preparing medicines and wearing:','["gloves", "jewelry", "sandals", "a hat only"]'::jsonb,0,'Gloves and hand hygiene.','original'),
('127.483.d.5.G',4,'Never reusing a counting tray for different drugs without cleaning it helps prevent cross-contamination and:','["speed", "errors", "savings", "growth"]'::jsonb,1,'Clean trays prevent mix-ups.','original')
) as v(code, diff, prompt, choices, ans, expl, src)
join public.teks_items i on i.code = v.code and i.is_standard
join public.teks_documents d on d.id = i.document_id and d.subject = 'Career Development' and d.language = 'en'
on conflict (fingerprint) do nothing;
